@attribute [CustomPage("Components/Overlays/Overview")]

<h1>Overlays</h1>

<h2><code>ConfirmDialog</code></h2>
<p>A question over a scrim with a cancel and a confirm button. Cancel takes focus when it opens, and the Android back button raises <code>OnCancel</code>.</p>
<ul>
    <li><code>Title</code> and optional <code>Message</code>; <code>ConfirmText</code> and <code>CancelText</code> (Cancel).</li>
    <li><code>Danger</code> styles the confirm button as destructive.</li>
    <li><code>data-testid</code>: <code>TestId</code> on the scrim, with <code>-cancel</code> and <code>-confirm</code> on the buttons.</li>
</ul>

<h2><code>Sheet</code></h2>
<p>A bottom sheet over a scrim, with a handle and a title that names it. It slides up (not with reduced motion) and is at most <code>--sheet-max-width</code> wide. Tab stays inside it, and focus returns to the control that opened it. A tap on the scrim, Escape and the Android back button raise <code>OnClose</code>; the sheet stays open until the owner clears <code>Open</code>.</p>
<ul>
    <li><code>Open</code>, <code>Title</code> (heading and accessible name), <code>OnClose</code>, <code>ChildContent</code> for the body.</li>
    <li><code>data-testid</code>: <code>TestId</code> on the sheet, with <code>-scrim</code> and <code>-handle</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h2><code>SheetAction</code></h2>
<p>A tile for a sheet's body: an icon over a label, at least a touch target tall. Put the tiles in a grid the sheet's body provides.</p>
<ul>
    <li><code>Icon</code>, <code>Label</code>, <code>OnClick</code>; <code>TestId</code> on the button.</li>
</ul>

